    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32977" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτελ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέλος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>brought to an end, perfect,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγάθ᾽ ἐκτελῆ γενέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					218
				</span></i>
			; of corn, <i>ripe,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				466
			</span></i>; also of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤδη πεφυκότ᾽ ἐκτελῆ νεανίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					780
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				105
			</span></i> (lyr., s. v.l.). Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῶς</span>
			<i>in full, completely</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1116.9
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B. C.)</span>.</div>
